# P2P Secure File Sharing — Java Client

## Overview

This is the Java implementation of a P2P secure file sharing system built for CISC 468. It operates with the Python and Go clients in this repository using a shared protocol defined in [`protocol/protocol.md`](../protocol/protocol.md).

### Security Features

- **Mutual authentication** via Ed25519 identity keypairs with out-of-band fingerprint verification
- **Perfect forward secrecy** through ephemeral X25519 key exchange (fresh keypair per connection)
- **Encrypted transport** using AES-256-GCM with session keys derived via HKDF-SHA256
- **File integrity** verification using SHA-256 hashes
- **Encrypted local storage** with AES-256-GCM (storage key derived from user passphrase via PBKDF2)
- **Key migration** with dual-signature verification (old key signs new, new key signs old)

### Libraries

| Library | Version | Purpose |
|---------|---------|---------|
| Bouncy Castle (`bcprov-jdk18on`) | 1.80 | Ed25519, X25519, HKDF-SHA256 |
| Gson | 2.11.0 | JSON serialization for protocol messages |
| JmDNS | 3.6.0 | mDNS peer discovery on the local network |
| JUnit 5 | 5.11.4 | Automated testing |

## Prerequisites

- Java 17+
- Maven 3.8+

## Build and Run

```
cd java-nick
mvn clean package -DskipTests -q
java -jar target/p2p-file-sharing-1.0-SNAPSHOT.jar
```

## Running Tests

```
mvn test
```

37 tests covering:

- **Crypto unit tests** — Ed25519 sign/verify, X25519 key agreement, AES-256-GCM encrypt/decrypt, HKDF derivation
- **Networking tests** — length-prefixed message framing, multi-message exchange, UTF-8 support
- **Integration tests** — full mutual authentication handshake (trusted and untrusted peers), chunked file transfer with SHA-256 verification, tamper detection, encrypted storage round-trip, key migration with dual-signature verification

## Architecture

```
src/main/java/com/p2pfs/
├── App.java                 # CLI entry point and session orchestration
├── crypto/
│   ├── Identity.java        # Ed25519 keypair management, sign/verify, fingerprints
│   ├── KeyExchange.java     # Ephemeral X25519 Diffie-Hellman key exchange
│   ├── SessionCipher.java   # AES-256-GCM session encryption/decryption
│   ├── Hkdf.java            # HKDF-SHA256 key derivation (RFC 5869)
│   └── FileHash.java        # SHA-256 file hashing and integrity verification
├── net/
│   ├── TcpServer.java       # TCP listener, accepts incoming peer connections
│   ├── TcpClient.java       # TCP connector for outgoing connections
│   ├── MessageFramer.java   # Length-prefixed (4-byte big-endian) JSON framing over TCP
│   └── PeerSession.java     # Authenticated session: handshake, encrypted send/receive
├── discovery/
│   └── MdnsService.java     # mDNS service registration and peer browsing via JmDNS
├── protocol/
│   ├── MessageType.java     # Enum of all protocol message types
│   ├── Messages.java        # Message POJOs and JSON serialization
│   └── ProtocolConstants.java
├── trust/
│   ├── TrustStore.java      # Persistent trusted contacts (JSON file)
│   └── KeyMigration.java    # Key migration message creation and verification
├── storage/
│   └── EncryptedFileStore.java  # AES-256-GCM encrypted file storage with PBKDF2 key derivation
└── sharing/
    ├── FileManager.java     # Local file tracking, hash computation, file list generation
    ├── FileListCache.java   # Caches peer file lists for offline peer lookup
    └── ConsentManager.java  # CLI consent prompts for file requests and offers
```

## CLI Usage

On startup, the application prompts for a peer name and storage passphrase, generates or loads an Ed25519 identity keypair, and begins listening for TCP connections and broadcasting via mDNS.

| Command | Description |
|---------|-------------|
| `peers` | List peers discovered on the local network via mDNS |
| `connect <name>` | Initiate a TCP connection and perform mutual authentication |
| `list <name>` | Request a peer's shared file list (no consent required) |
| `request <name> <file>` | Request a file from a peer (requires their consent) |
| `send <name> <filepath>` | Offer a file to a peer (requires their consent) |
| `migrate` | Generate a new identity keypair and notify connected peers |
| `contacts` | Display all trusted contacts and their fingerprints |
| `exit` | Shut down the application |

Files to share are placed in `data/<peer-name>/shared/`. Received files are saved to the same directory and also stored encrypted in `data/<peer-name>/store/`.

## Protocol

All three clients (Java, Python, Go) implement the same wire protocol. See [`protocol/protocol.md`](../protocol/protocol.md) for the full specification, including message formats, handshake flow, and security considerations.
